From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: a heap refusal of an image's or a buffer's slot is a refusal like the device's, not the end (KEEPS THE STORE)

Store: KEEPS THE STORE. vk_texture_cache.h and buffer_cache.h change; neither is among the
translation id's inputs; no switch name is added to TranslationSwitches (EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS
is read as before, unchanged).

A pure fix, no switch: where the program ended, an image or a buffer is now left out.

Why: run1395's std::bad_alloc came out of SlotVector<Image>::insert inside
TextureCacheRuntime::SurvivesImageRefusal (JoinImages' make_image; symbols of T166's llvm-pie.elf),
which catches only the device's VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY. With the console's SlotVector now
letting a refused growth out with nothing changed (0890 + front slot_vector_recovery.cmake), the
two places that already have a refusal path take it:
- SurvivesImageRefusal: std::bad_alloc (the slot, or what the image's constructor asks of the heap)
  is a refusal like the device's: the image is left out ("No memory for the image ... left out",
  1 s pause for that size and larger), and EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT, when on, deletes old images
  (which frees slots) and tries once more. With EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS (or UNBACKED_LIMIT) it
  ends the session as before.
- BufferCache::JoinBuffer: a refused slot destroys the buffer just made and returns the refusal
  (CreateRefusedBuffer, as when the device says no); the holes path drops that buffer (counted in
  buffers_dropped, as now).
Lines (stderr): "EDEN_UP_TABLE_REFUSED image <n>: ..." / "... buffer <n>: ..." for the first 8 of each,
then every 64th.

What it does not cover: the other tables (views, allocations, framebuffers, samplers, map views)
have no refusal path; a refused growth there still ends the program (0891 reserves them).
Not checked: a build, the console, a run where the heap refuses an image's slot.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 1e09175c30..48c8ddf5c1 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <memory>
+#include <new>
 #include <numeric>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <utility>
@@ -44,6 +45,18 @@ namespace VideoCommon {
 
 using Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE;
 
+// 0892: a stderr line for the first 8 buffers whose slot the heap refused, then every 64th.
+inline void NoteHeapRefusedBuffer() noexcept {
+    static std::atomic<u64> refused{0};
+    const u64 count = refused.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+    if (count <= 8 || (count & 63) == 0) {
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "EDEN_UP_TABLE_REFUSED buffer %llu: the heap refused its slot; refused as "
+                     "the device's\n",
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(count));
+    }
+}
+
 template <class P>
 BufferCache<P>::BufferCache(Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManager& device_memory_, Runtime& runtime_)
     : runtime{runtime_}, device_memory{device_memory_}, memory_tracker{device_memory} {
@@ -5081,6 +5094,18 @@ BufferId BufferCache<P>::JoinBuffer(DAddr device_addr, u32 wanted_size, bool spa
                 buffer_refused_size = size;
             }
         }
+        if (made) [[likely]] {
+            // 0892: the heap may refuse the slot (the table doubling in one allocation; on the
+            // console SlotVector lets that out with nothing changed, as in run1395's image
+            // table, headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake). Then the buffer goes (its memory with
+            // it) and this is a refusal like the device's: CreateRefusedBuffer.
+            try {
+                new_buffer_id = slot_buffers.insert(std::move(*made));
+            } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+                made.reset();
+                NoteHeapRefusedBuffer();
+            }
+        }
         if (!made) [[unlikely]] {
             // Nothing else has changed: the buffers stay as they are, and they stay findable.
             for (const BufferId overlap_id : overlap.ids) {
@@ -5088,7 +5113,6 @@ BufferId BufferCache<P>::JoinBuffer(DAddr device_addr, u32 wanted_size, bool spa
             }
             return BufferId{};
         }
-        new_buffer_id = slot_buffers.insert(std::move(*made));
     } else {
         new_buffer_id = slot_buffers.insert(runtime, overlap.begin, size, sparse_compatible);
     }
@@ -5187,7 +5211,13 @@ BufferId BufferCache<P>::CreateRefusedBuffer(DAddr device_addr, u32 wanted_size,
             buffer_hole_refused = bytes;
             continue;
         }
-        const BufferId id = slot_buffers.insert(std::move(*made));
+        BufferId id;
+        try {
+            id = slot_buffers.insert(std::move(*made)); // 0892: as in JoinBuffer
+        } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+            NoteHeapRefusedBuffer();
+            break;
+        }
         Churn::Add(Churn::BuffersCreated);
         Buffer& buffer = slot_buffers[id];
         runtime.ClearBuffer(buffer, 0, bytes, 0);
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
index 6ad558c09a..22d2da4afa 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
@@ -6,9 +6,12 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <chrono>
+#include <cstdio>
 #include <deque>
 #include <memory>
+#include <new>
 #include <optional>
 #include <span>
 #include <utility>
@@ -92,6 +95,30 @@ public:
                 throw;
             }
             return false;
+        } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+            // 0892: the heap refused the image's slot (the table doubling: run1395, 13 Nov, one
+            // 10,354,696 byte request on GPUBack) or something the image's constructor asks for.
+            // On the console SlotVector lets that out with nothing changed
+            // (headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake); it is the same as a device refusal: the image
+            // is left out, and the caller's EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT, if on, frees slots and tries
+            // once more. Ends the session as before with EDEN_NX2_IMAGE_REFUSED_ENDS.
+            if (ImageRefusalEnds()) {
+                throw;
+            }
+            NoteHeapRefusedImage();
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// 0892: a stderr line for the first 8 images the heap refused, then every 64th (count only).
+    static void NoteHeapRefusedImage() noexcept {
+        static std::atomic<u64> refused{0};
+        const u64 count = refused.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+        if (count <= 8 || (count & 63) == 0) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_UP_TABLE_REFUSED image %llu: the heap refused it (its slot or its "
+                         "records); left out\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(count));
         }
     }
 
